WEBVTT

00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:10.220
Monitoring actuator operation.

00:02:10.220 --> 00:02:11.880
Power transfer link, condition green.

00:02:12.490 --> 00:02:15.360
Is the time base corrector
functioning properly?

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:17.260
All green. Working correctly.

00:02:17.260 --> 00:02:20.030
We're going to add on the data
we collected in Belgistan,

00:02:20.030 --> 00:02:22.760
please conduct a pattern C simulation.

00:02:22.760 --> 00:02:24.960
There seems to be little fluctuation

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:26.970
in the movement patterns.

00:02:26.970 --> 00:02:28.400
Then we'll adjust the
algorithm of stage B.

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:30.500
Yes? Lieutenant Colonel Hirokawa?
Then we'll adjust the
algorithm of stage B.

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:31.300
But first,

00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:31.600
can't we conduct a simulation of
the target acquisition pattern?

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:34.470
Yes, understood, today.
can't we conduct a simulation of
the target acquisition pattern?

00:02:34.470 --> 00:02:34.940
I'll make sure to be there.
can't we conduct a simulation of
the target acquisition pattern?

00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:37.340
I'll change the threshold level of
the thermal imagery system.

00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:37.340
I'll make sure to be there.

00:02:37.940 --> 00:02:39.780
Yeah, I think there was
definite improvement

00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:42.750
in the realism of the stereoscopic
holograph imagery.

00:02:43.380 --> 00:02:46.720
I'd say about a 15% improvement
in overall visibility.

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:47.890
That's a ballpark, of course.

00:02:47.890 --> 00:02:48.220
Please refrain from making
unqualified assessments.
That's a ballpark, of course.

00:02:48.220 --> 00:02:50.460
Please refrain from making
unqualified assessments.

00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:54.260
I'd like all of you to pause and
listen to what I have to say.

00:02:54.260 --> 00:02:57.160
I just received word from
Colonel Hirokawa.

00:02:57.160 --> 00:02:59.770
He's asking me to meet Mr. Nishida.

00:02:59.770 --> 00:03:01.330
This probably will entail a discussion

00:03:01.330 --> 00:03:04.170
on securing the support of the TA
experimentation company.

00:03:04.170 --> 00:03:06.240
What are they trying to do?

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:09.500
I'm not sure myself.

00:03:11.480 --> 00:03:13.070
What do you intend to do, Sir?

00:03:14.110 --> 00:03:17.180
Whatever it is, I'm intent on declining.

00:03:17.180 --> 00:03:19.220
But nevertheless, I don't
want my decision

00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:21.750
to commit you to something
you do not wish to do.

00:03:21.750 --> 00:03:24.190
If you have any requests, or
wish to voice any views...

00:03:24.190 --> 00:03:26.290
Please, Sir. You don't have
to worry about that.

00:03:26.290 --> 00:03:28.350
You are our leader, Colonel.

00:03:32.970 --> 00:03:37.240
So, the SSDF was deployed into the
community where Won lives?

00:03:37.240 --> 00:03:40.400
Yes, Sir, but we haven't received
word from Won since.

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:46.710
Get me General Armor
at the Pentagon.

00:03:46.710 --> 00:03:48.870
The Pentagon, Sir?

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:52.080
It's time we put together
a contingency plan.

00:04:02.530 --> 00:04:04.000
Colonel Hayakawa...

00:04:04.730 --> 00:04:07.400
Mr. Nishida is expecting you inside.

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:08.870
Excuse me.

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:12.770
I've been expecting you,
Colonel Hayakawa.

00:04:15.580 --> 00:04:17.940
Just look at yourself, pressing
your luck like this.

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:20.180
You're fortunate not to be dead.

00:04:20.180 --> 00:04:22.110
For good or bad, I always get a break.

00:04:22.750 --> 00:04:25.990
Well, I guess you're okay as long
as you're talking like that.

00:04:25.990 --> 00:04:29.180
I'll be downstairs. Let me know
if you need anything.

00:04:33.260 --> 00:04:35.190
Mr. Won, I'm really sorry about this.

00:04:35.190 --> 00:04:38.200
You became injured while
you were helping us.

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:41.230
This isn't your fault.
All of this was rigged.

00:04:41.230 --> 00:04:44.300
That riot took place because
someone wanted it to,

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:47.710
and the deployment of that robot
to this neighborhood

00:04:47.710 --> 00:04:49.910
was orchestrated by someone
in advance.

00:04:49.910 --> 00:04:51.380
Orchestrated?

00:04:51.950 --> 00:04:54.380
We were setup to be the scapegoat.

00:04:54.950 --> 00:04:57.440
All so that the rioting
could be contained.

00:04:58.650 --> 00:05:01.850
But people live here like they
do anywhere else.

00:05:01.850 --> 00:05:04.560
This neighborhood is full of both
the happiness and sorrow

00:05:04.560 --> 00:05:06.230
that comes with people
living out their lives,

00:05:06.230 --> 00:05:08.090
as best they can, day
after day, everyday.

00:05:11.630 --> 00:05:13.500
I understand.

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:16.300
You're planning on leaving, aren't you?

00:05:17.570 --> 00:05:19.040
Where do you plan to go?

00:05:20.010 --> 00:05:21.770
Tokyo.

00:05:21.770 --> 00:05:24.300
So, you'll be right under their noses?

00:05:25.080 --> 00:05:27.210
But right now is not the time.

00:05:27.210 --> 00:05:29.820
I don't know how you were planning
on making it there,

00:05:29.820 --> 00:05:32.510
but you won't be able to
make it by yourselves.

00:05:33.350 --> 00:05:34.950
Let our people help you.

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:36.920
Your people?

00:05:36.920 --> 00:05:37.020
Hey, the wolf knows what the
monster thinks, right?
Your people?

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:40.130
Hey, the wolf knows what the
monster thinks, right?

00:05:40.130 --> 00:05:42.490
There are some services available only
to those in the underground.

00:05:43.860 --> 00:05:45.630
Colonel Hayakawa,

00:05:45.630 --> 00:05:49.540
you probably know already why
you were asked to come here.

00:05:49.540 --> 00:05:51.000
Generally speaking, yes.

00:05:56.080 --> 00:05:57.640
A moratorium?

00:05:57.640 --> 00:06:01.310
Yes, a full and unilateral suspension
of all grain exports.

00:06:01.910 --> 00:06:03.580
I'm certain that the US government

00:06:03.580 --> 00:06:07.120
will announce this policy
within a day or two.

00:06:07.120 --> 00:06:09.350
America would not dare do
something like that!

00:06:10.620 --> 00:06:13.720
Japan's food self-sufficiency is at 40%.

00:06:15.400 --> 00:06:17.460
If they went ahead with this...

00:06:17.460 --> 00:06:19.520
A depression will undoubtedly
come about.

00:06:20.200 --> 00:06:22.760
So we must do everything we can
to prevent this from happening.

00:06:23.800 --> 00:06:26.570
How can you prevent something
like this, unless...

00:06:27.540 --> 00:06:30.680
Yes, there is only one solution
to this situation,

00:06:30.680 --> 00:06:34.040
and that is what we are
attempting to do.

00:06:39.190 --> 00:06:41.980
The US Marine Corps anti-terrorist
special forces...

00:06:42.520 --> 00:06:45.260
Thank you very much. I'm
deeply indebted to you.

00:06:45.260 --> 00:06:46.730
Later then.

00:06:47.860 --> 00:06:51.350
In the end, I seem to be left with a
debt to repay to the Pentagon.

00:06:54.230 --> 00:06:57.360
Yes, but will the international
community accept this?

00:06:57.940 --> 00:07:01.340
I'm certain that an attempt
will be launched,

00:07:01.340 --> 00:07:04.340
with the US at its head,
to interfere with this.

00:07:04.340 --> 00:07:07.780
But I will make certain that nothing
more will come about.

00:07:07.780 --> 00:07:10.040
I will protect Japan!

00:07:17.260 --> 00:07:17.360
Say, about that guy from the
district attorney's office...

00:07:17.360 --> 00:07:20.330
Say, about that guy from the
