00:07:49.790 --> 00:07:54.260
Colonel Hayakawa, why did you
become a member of the SSDF?

00:07:54.260 --> 00:07:55.760
Well...

00:07:55.760 --> 00:07:59.930
You're not a person to become part of
the SSDF without a good reason.

00:08:00.630 --> 00:08:03.000
Hirokawa is much the same.

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:04.470
He is not simply seduced
by the concept

00:08:04.470 --> 00:08:08.640
of protecting and ensuring the
integrity of the nation.

00:08:08.640 --> 00:08:12.650
The land that gave birth to us,
that brought us up.

00:08:12.650 --> 00:08:15.380
When he thought back about this
affinity that arises naturally

00:08:15.380 --> 00:08:21.320
toward your own homeland, an
ideal manifests within himself.

00:08:21.320 --> 00:08:25.280
Hirokawa joined the SSDF as a
way to answer to that ideal.

00:08:26.690 --> 00:08:28.460
That's what he said to me.

00:08:29.700 --> 00:08:33.860
But to remain true to your ideals
is an arduous path to confront.

00:08:34.630 --> 00:08:36.300
Everyday, reality rears its ugly head,

00:08:36.300 --> 00:08:40.140
and imposes tremendous obstacles in
your quest to realize your ideal.

00:08:40.140 --> 00:08:43.480
But does not society prosper from the
process of vigorous competition

00:08:43.480 --> 00:08:46.080
between different ideals?

00:08:46.080 --> 00:08:49.780
Ideals do not crush ideals.

00:08:49.780 --> 00:08:54.150
Only ignorance born of indifferent
apathy does.

00:08:54.150 --> 00:08:55.590
Apathy?

00:08:55.590 --> 00:08:55.660
Colonel Hayakawa,
Apathy?

00:08:55.660 --> 00:08:57.290
Colonel Hayakawa,

00:08:57.290 --> 00:09:01.120
I would like you to examine us by
the values that you hold dear,

00:09:01.660 --> 00:09:03.830
and then judge us accordingly.

00:09:03.830 --> 00:09:07.100
But what of the law? What of the
upholding of law and order?

00:09:07.100 --> 00:09:08.790
The law?

00:09:09.640 --> 00:09:10.940
When we look back on history,

00:09:10.940 --> 00:09:14.440
laws have not provided people with
answers to issues confronting them.

00:09:14.440 --> 00:09:16.740
In the end, only people
can resolve issues.

00:09:16.740 --> 00:09:18.680
People?

00:09:19.210 --> 00:09:22.320
The announcement by the Department
of Agriculture will be made at nine am

00:09:22.320 --> 00:09:26.650
which translates to eleven o'clock
tomorrow night Japan time.

00:09:26.650 --> 00:09:28.120
Yes, thank you.

00:09:30.120 --> 00:09:33.610
Now the last hammer is
about to come down.

00:09:49.210 --> 00:09:50.680
Mr. Won!

00:09:51.740 --> 00:09:53.910
Are you all right, getting up like this?

00:09:53.910 --> 00:09:55.950
Yes, I'm fine,

00:09:55.950 --> 00:09:58.470
but there is something I need
to ask you about.

00:10:00.420 --> 00:10:01.890
It's about that girl.

00:10:03.020 --> 00:10:07.230
A colossal organization is using
all they have to find that girl.

00:10:07.230 --> 00:10:08.760
You mean Symbol?

00:10:08.760 --> 00:10:10.330
You know about them?

00:10:10.330 --> 00:10:14.060
Then I'll cut right to the point.
Who is that girl?

00:10:14.970 --> 00:10:17.700
Miharu is just like me.

00:10:18.400 --> 00:10:21.170
She was a TA pilot with Symbol.

00:10:21.170 --> 00:10:22.830
Impossible, but...

00:10:23.580 --> 00:10:26.350
Well, that explains why a
member of the Council

00:10:26.350 --> 00:10:28.150
would come all the way out here.

00:10:28.150 --> 00:10:30.950
But how did you two hook up?

00:10:30.950 --> 00:10:34.750
We realized that we were nothing
more than a means to an end.

00:10:34.750 --> 00:10:38.290
Tools they employ to accomplish
their ambitions.

00:10:38.290 --> 00:10:39.760
Tools?

00:10:44.130 --> 00:10:47.830
I'm sorry about asking tough
questions like that.

00:10:47.830 --> 00:10:49.360
No, that's okay.

00:10:54.410 --> 00:10:55.870
Yushiro...

00:10:56.610 --> 00:10:58.080
Never mind...

00:11:01.010 --> 00:11:03.040
Tools? They're just
like I used to be.

00:11:14.760 --> 00:11:16.230
Orders, Sir.

00:11:26.210 --> 00:11:27.670
What are you doing here?

00:11:29.510 --> 00:11:32.850
The Colonel hasn't returned yet.
He wouldn't...

00:11:32.850 --> 00:11:35.970
Don't worry. I trust the Colonel.

00:12:02.170 --> 00:12:04.840
That concludes the summary on the
training program here.

00:12:04.840 --> 00:12:06.510
Are there any questions?

00:12:06.510 --> 00:12:07.580
Sir?

00:12:07.580 --> 00:12:08.010
Yes?
Sir?

00:12:08.010 --> 00:12:09.040
Yes?

00:12:09.650 --> 00:12:12.580
You mentioned that we
must be proud.

00:12:13.120 --> 00:12:15.420
What do you mean by pride, Sir?

00:12:15.420 --> 00:12:17.660
What are you trying to say?

00:12:17.660 --> 00:12:21.920
Sir, I believe that pride comes
about from pursuing a goal.

00:12:22.460 --> 00:12:24.160
A goal, in other words,

00:12:24.160 --> 00:12:27.560
what do we seek and what do
we attempt to accomplish.

00:12:28.170 --> 00:12:30.870
Would you be kind enough to
express what this mission is?

00:12:30.870 --> 00:12:32.810
It can be your own personal
definition, Sir.

00:12:32.810 --> 00:12:34.440
I see.

00:12:34.440 --> 00:12:35.910
I suppose...

00:12:36.640 --> 00:12:39.980
Those who join the SSDF will be
questioning themselves everyday,

00:12:39.980 --> 00:12:43.350
constantly about what
they should do.

00:12:44.050 --> 00:12:46.520
However, many will quit, unable
to find that answer.

00:12:46.520 --> 00:12:52.860
Others will compromise and
stop seeking an answer.

00:12:53.430 --> 00:12:59.830
But most will continue to question,
and retire without an answer.

00:12:59.830 --> 00:13:05.370
I must admit, I am also one of those
who continue to question.

00:13:05.370 --> 00:13:09.410
But recently, I am beginning
to think that it is all right.

00:13:09.410 --> 00:13:11.680
Why? Because by constantly
questioning,

00:13:11.680 --> 00:13:14.010
I feel that I come that much
closer to discovering

00:13:14.010 --> 00:13:16.850
what it is that I am seeking.

00:13:17.880 --> 00:13:21.150
Now, just don't start asking me
what that ideal is, okay?

00:13:23.360 --> 00:13:26.660
Do you mind if I pose the same
question back to you?

00:13:26.660 --> 00:13:28.390
I entered into service
because I felt that,

00:13:28.390 --> 00:13:32.870
by joining an organization that tries
to define its own mission,

00:13:32.870 --> 00:13:37.130
I might learn what the Japanese
people seek for themselves.

00:13:38.470 --> 00:13:40.340
What the Japanese people
seek for themselves?

00:13:41.710 --> 00:13:44.470
I think I found that person
you were looking for,

00:13:45.210 --> 00:13:47.380
but now is not a good time.

00:13:47.380 --> 00:13:50.880
This place is crawling with
cops and SSDF.

00:13:50.880 --> 00:13:54.820
The council member says that, if you
can meet his expectations,

00:13:54.820 --> 00:13:58.290
he'll have you invited back into
our organization again.

00:13:58.290 --> 00:13:59.860
Invite me back?

00:13:59.860 --> 00:14:03.130
I'm sure you would not want to miss
out on a chance like this one.

00:14:03.130 --> 00:14:06.230
Three days, no, give me two days.

00:14:06.230 --> 00:14:08.270
I'll try to get something
together by then.

00:14:08.270 --> 00:14:09.630
Don't let us down.

00:14:12.170 --> 00:14:14.140
Give me another chance?

00:14:15.140 --> 00:14:17.480
It looks like he took the bait.

00:14:17.480 --> 00:14:18.940
I'm not so sure about that.

00:14:19.650 --> 00:14:22.840
Two days, which must mean he intends
to make his move today.

00:14:23.920 --> 00:14:26.040
I suppose it would not hurt
to play this safe.

00:14:28.250 --> 00:14:32.880
You are to remain inside until we hear
of movement by our target.

00:14:44.470 --> 00:14:46.230
Mr. Nishida, you are...

00:14:47.340 --> 00:14:48.310
Move out now?

00:14:48.310 --> 00:14:52.550
Yeah, I'm sure Symbol will make their
move in two or three days.

00:14:52.550 --> 00:14:54.250
We're going to clear out of here
before that happens.

00:14:54.250 --> 00:14:58.080
We have a ship waiting
for you in the harbor.

00:14:58.080 --> 00:15:00.620
It will take you to Tokyo.

00:15:00.620 --> 00:15:02.780
Let's get your stuff together.

00:15:03.760 --> 00:15:04.790
I already have everything together.

00:15:04.790 --> 00:15:05.260
You were ready for this, weren't you?
I already have everything together.

00:15:05.260 --> 00:15:06.360
You were ready for this, weren't you?

00:15:06.360 --> 00:15:08.550
You must have been anticipating
this for awhile.

00:15:09.160 --> 00:15:10.790
Miharu, let's go.

00:15:13.370 --> 00:15:15.700
Right now Lee is helping with
the loading of the ship.

00:15:15.700 --> 00:15:17.240
I know this will be uncomfortable,

00:15:17.240 --> 00:15:19.360
but we're going to hide you there
until you get to the docks.

00:15:20.070 --> 00:15:22.510
They're going to make it out of here
if it's the last thing I do!

00:15:26.650 --> 00:15:28.140
The situation has become dangerous?

00:15:28.780 --> 00:15:30.980
I fear my master's health will
not last much longer.

00:15:30.980 --> 00:15:34.320
Mr. Nishida, I just have
one question to ask.

00:15:34.850 --> 00:15:38.520
Do you believe in this country
we know as Japan?

00:15:38.520 --> 00:15:40.360
Yes, I do.

00:15:40.360 --> 00:15:43.360
But how can you place your trust in
this nation in its current state?

00:15:43.360 --> 00:15:46.200
Colonel Hayakawa, no matter
what anyone else may say,

00:15:46.200 --> 00:15:48.970
nothing can change the fact
that I am Japanese.

00:15:48.970 --> 00:15:50.440
Japanese?

00:15:52.440 --> 00:15:53.570
Who is it?

00:15:53.570 --> 00:15:53.940
It is I.
Who is it?

00:15:53.940 --> 00:15:55.110
It is I.

00:15:55.110 --> 00:15:57.810
Hirokawa, I demand you keep out!

00:15:57.810 --> 00:16:00.070
I'm sorry, I was just anxious...

00:16:01.010 --> 00:16:04.540
No, I apologize. I understand
how you feel.

00:16:05.220 --> 00:16:08.620
Please understand, Colonel Hayakawa
and I are having a discussion

00:16:08.620 --> 00:16:11.620
where we hold back nothing, showing
everything about ourselves.

00:16:11.620 --> 00:16:14.290
That's why I beg that you let
us remain in seclusion.

00:16:17.500 --> 00:16:20.170
I must apologize for my crudeness.

00:16:20.170 --> 00:16:21.760
Mr. Nishida, that katana...

00:16:23.100 --> 00:16:26.470
Colonel Hayakawa, I pray that you
do not misunderstand me.

00:16:31.080 --> 00:16:32.410
Please behold.

00:16:32.410 --> 00:16:35.110
This luminescent blade, pristine
like untouched spring water.

00:16:35.110 --> 00:16:36.580
But its current form

00:16:36.580 --> 00:16:39.390
is the culmination of evolution
forced upon it

00:16:39.390 --> 00:16:41.190
by successive countless battles
over many centuries,

00:16:41.190 --> 00:16:45.350
realized only by triumphing over
each challenge it faced.

00:16:46.130 --> 00:16:47.330
Its crystal clear quality represents

00:16:47.330 --> 00:16:50.360
the essence of the Japanese spirit
now largely forgotten.

00:16:50.360 --> 00:16:54.430
For this reason, what I hold in my
hand is not a weapon, but my soul.

00:16:54.430 --> 00:16:57.630
How can one brandish one's
soul against another?

00:16:58.240 --> 00:17:01.930
You can only brandish that
soul against yourself.

00:17:02.980 --> 00:17:05.840
Mr. Nishida, you weren't thinking of...

00:17:07.680 --> 00:17:10.320
I was intent on ending my own life

00:17:10.320 --> 00:17:12.650
if I could not convince you to join us.

00:17:13.350 --> 00:17:17.220
But I ask that you do not take that
into account over this matter.

00:17:17.920 --> 00:17:21.650
I want you to base it on your own
judgment as guided by your heart.

00:17:33.640 --> 00:17:37.800
I'd like to assist in realizing
your ideal, Mr. Nishida.

00:17:41.310 --> 00:17:42.820
I wonder if they'll be safe?

00:17:42.820 --> 00:17:46.190
I'm sure of it. Mr. Won is with them.

00:17:46.190 --> 00:17:49.250
Yes, they went ahead and left today.

00:17:49.250 --> 00:17:51.420
Roger that. We're taking
off immediately.

00:17:56.530 --> 00:17:58.430
Now it should be smooth sailing.

00:17:58.430 --> 00:18:02.200
I don't think that robot will be able
to come after us over water.

00:18:09.140 --> 00:18:13.080
So, what do you plan on doing
once you get back to Tokyo?

00:18:13.080 --> 00:18:15.680
I'm going to try to find my friends.

00:18:15.680 --> 00:18:16.380
Friends?

00:18:16.380 --> 00:18:17.180
Yes, my friends in the SSDF.
Friends?

00:18:17.180 --> 00:18:18.850
Yes, my friends in the SSDF.

00:18:18.850 --> 00:18:21.250
Friends? That sounds
like a good idea.

00:18:21.250 --> 00:18:24.520
No matter how much you try, you
can only go so far by yourself.

00:18:25.060 --> 00:18:26.890
That girl...

00:18:26.890 --> 00:18:28.360
What's that?!

00:18:47.780 --> 00:18:49.250
Yushiro!

00:19:16.440 --> 00:19:17.910
Stay away!

00:19:29.050 --> 00:19:29.790
Come back!

00:19:29.790 --> 00:19:30.560
Hold it right there! Let that girl go!
Come back!

00:19:30.560 --> 00:19:32.420
Hold it right there! Let that girl go!

00:19:39.060 --> 00:19:40.930
Mr. Won!

00:19:40.930 --> 00:19:42.400
Come back here!

00:19:45.040 --> 00:19:46.500
Miharu!

00:19:48.140 --> 00:19:49.770
Miharu!

00:19:54.750 --> 00:19:56.840
Sure wish I could've kept my promise.

00:19:57.450 --> 00:20:00.050
I'm really sorry, you know.

00:20:00.050 --> 00:20:01.990
Mr. Won, you have to keep quiet.

00:20:01.990 --> 00:20:03.920
No, it's all right.

00:20:03.920 --> 00:20:05.450
But about that girl...

00:20:06.390 --> 00:20:08.290
Mr. Won!

00:20:08.290 --> 00:20:11.130
It was Symbol.

00:20:11.130 --> 00:20:12.600
Meth...

00:20:13.500 --> 00:20:14.970
What a sad sack I am.

00:20:15.900 --> 00:20:17.570
Mr. Won!

00:20:17.570 --> 00:20:19.300
Mr. Won! Mr. Won!

00:20:25.980 --> 00:20:28.410
We've secured the TA company,

00:20:28.410 --> 00:20:31.450
but we're concerned about the
health of Mr. Nishida.

00:20:31.450 --> 00:20:34.490
He spent two days straight trying
to convince the Colonel

00:20:34.490 --> 00:20:36.690
without food or rest.

00:20:36.690 --> 00:20:39.180
Yes, he's resting at the moment.

00:20:40.330 --> 00:20:41.660
What? Tonight?

00:20:41.660 --> 00:20:41.830
Yes, the moratorium will be made
public at 11 o'clock Japan time.
What? Tonight?

00:20:41.830 --> 00:20:46.390
Yes, the moratorium will be made
public at 11 o'clock Japan time.

00:20:46.800 --> 00:20:51.170
Understood. I'll head directly to
the Prime Minister from here.

00:20:51.170 --> 00:20:54.510
...announced a moratorium to be in
effect for the next twelve months.

00:20:54.510 --> 00:20:57.210
Super 821 has been declared,

00:20:57.210 --> 00:20:58.340
bringing related agricultural products
under economic control.

00:20:58.340 --> 00:21:00.950
This policy is having a profound
impact all around the globe.

00:21:00.950 --> 00:21:02.450
Already, other grain
exporting nations...

00:21:02.450 --> 00:21:04.320
...on the New York Stock Exchange,
as the circuit breakers

00:21:04.320 --> 00:21:06.490
which prevent a market collapse...

00:21:06.490 --> 00:21:08.450
The Cabinet of Prime Minister
Munakata is urging the Japanese

00:21:08.450 --> 00:21:10.920
to remain calm following this dramatic
announcement by the U.S.

00:21:10.920 --> 00:21:13.590
The situation calls for
drastic measures.

00:21:13.590 --> 00:21:15.460
Sir, we have no time to waste.

00:21:16.060 --> 00:21:18.430
So, what do you want me to do?

00:21:18.960 --> 00:21:21.070
You must issue the executive order

00:21:21.070 --> 00:21:22.630
authorizing the General Economy
Controls Measures

00:21:22.630 --> 00:21:25.370
and mobilize the SSDF to prevent
the outbreak of further rioting.

00:21:25.370 --> 00:21:27.030
But that would mean...

00:21:28.040 --> 00:21:30.740
And even if I did, how
long will it take to...

00:21:30.740 --> 00:21:32.710
I've already made the necessary
preparations, Prime Minister.

00:21:33.610 --> 00:21:36.670
Lieutenant Colonel Hirokawa,
what's going on here?

00:21:48.960 --> 00:21:50.430
What the hell?

00:21:51.660 --> 00:21:53.300
This just in.

00:21:53.300 --> 00:21:56.300
At 2: 15 this morning, in response to
the American grain moratorium

00:21:56.300 --> 00:21:57.840
the Government has issued an
executive order

00:21:57.840 --> 00:22:00.610
authorizing the General Economic
Control Measures...

00:22:00.610 --> 00:22:02.340
A dawn to dusk curfew
has been issued

00:22:02.340 --> 00:22:05.840
as part of riot prevention measures
for the next seven days.

00:22:05.840 --> 00:22:07.210
I repeat...

00:22:07.210 --> 00:22:09.650
At last, martial law is being declared.

00:22:10.280 --> 00:22:11.650
City residents are instructed

00:22:11.650 --> 00:22:15.250
to remain indoors until 6 o'clock
tomorrow morning.

00:22:15.250 --> 00:22:18.450
Anyone found to be in violation of
the curfew will be detained.

00:22:28.510 --> 00:22:33.330
Hark

00:22:34.590 --> 00:22:39.880
It's time I journey

00:22:43.410 --> 00:22:50.550
Break apart my heart

00:22:50.720 --> 00:22:57.080
For crimson sadness

00:22:57.410 --> 00:23:04.590
Pours out from it

00:23:04.800 --> 00:23:08.510
I can only, oh

00:23:08.620 --> 00:23:11.700
Close my eyes, oh

00:23:11.790 --> 00:23:17.310
I pray, let this break apart

00:23:32.530 --> 00:23:36.410
I can only, oh

00:23:36.500 --> 00:23:39.560
Close my eyes, oh

00:23:39.630 --> 00:23:44.760
I pray, let this break apart

00:23:46.290 --> 00:23:52.740
I beg you, be by my side

00:24:00.130 --> 00:24:01.920
Each has their own feelings.

00:24:02.460 --> 00:24:04.800
Each has their own wishes.

00:24:04.800 --> 00:24:07.960
Perplexed and anxious, all of us
ask ourselves questions

00:24:08.630 --> 00:24:10.640
about the path we took.

00:24:10.640 --> 00:24:12.470
Where we should aim for tomorrow.

00:24:12.470 --> 00:24:14.840
Individually we come to
make up our minds.

00:24:15.370 --> 00:24:17.310
But where am I?

00:24:18.010 --> 00:24:19.440
Here, adrift among

00:24:19.440 --> 00:24:21.980
Swelling waves of a world caught
in great upheaval

00:24:21.980 --> 00:24:24.510
Alone I pursue after the one
dearest to my heart

00:24:25.380 --> 00:24:27.370
I can't hold back these feelings.
